(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the morphological taxonomy of Greek and Latin roots, prefixes, and suffixes in biotechnology and life sciences.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Classical Linguistic Scaffolding of Scientific Lexis:) Tj
T*
(   Modern biotechnology nomenclature relies on Greek and Latin morphemes because classical roots) Tj
T*
(   provide semantic transparency, modular productivity, and international comprehension across) Tj
T*
(   linguistic boundaries.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Comprehensive Morphemic Inventory:) Tj
T*
(   - Root Morphemes:) Tj
T*
(   - Bio- \(Greek bios: life\): biochemistry, bioreactor, biodegradable, biotransformation.) Tj
T*
(   - Cyto- / -cyte \(Greek kytos: hollow vessel / cell\): cytoplasm, leukocyte, cytogenetics.) Tj
T*
(   - Geno- / Gen- \(Greek genos: birth, race, origin\): genome, genotype, pathogenesis.) Tj
T*
(   - Lyso- / -lysis \(Greek lysis: loosening / dissolution\): lysosome, glycolysis, proteolysis.) Tj
T*
(   - Morph- \(Greek morphe: form / shape\): morphology, amorphous, polymorphism.) Tj
T*
(   - Spatial and Relational Prefixes:) Tj
T*
(   - Endo- \(within\): endocytosis, endonuclease, endogenous.) Tj
T*
(   - Exo- / Ecto- \(outside\): exocytosis, exonuclease, ectopic expression.) Tj
T*
(   - Inter- \(between\): intercellular signaling, intermolecular forces.) Tj
T*
(   - Intra- \(within / inside\): intracellular trafficking, intraflagellar transport.) Tj
T*
(   - Hyper- \(above / excessive\): hyperthermophilic, hypersensitive, hyperglycemia.) Tj
T*
(   - Hypo- \(below / deficient\): hypotonic, hypomorphic allele.) Tj
T*
(   - Suffixal Classifiers:) Tj
T*
(   - -ase: Systematically designates an enzyme \(polymerase, kinase, ligase, amylase\).) Tj
T*
(   - -ome: Denotes the holistic totality of a biological system \(genome, proteome, transcriptome\).) Tj
T*
(   - -omics: The high-throughput analytical study of an -ome \(genomics, proteomics, metabolomics\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Contrast informal phrasal verbs with formal Latinate verbs in scientific publications, providing a comprehensive translation matrix.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Rhetorical Register Divide:) Tj
T*
(   Phrasal verbs \(base verb + prepositional or adverbial particle\) are native Germanic) Tj
T*
(   constructions characterized by informal, conversational vitality. However, formal academic peer) Tj
T*
(   review demands single-word Latinate or French-derived verbs that embody emotional detachment,) Tj
T*
(   semantic precision, and concision.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Comprehensive Academic Translation Matrix:) Tj
T*
(   - "carry out" -> conduct, execute, perform, implement) Tj
T*
(   - "find out" -> discover, determine, ascertain, deduce) Tj
T*
(   - "look into" -> investigate, examine, inspect, scrutinize) Tj
T*
(   - "break down" -> degrade, decompose, lyse, catabolize) Tj
T*
(   - "set up" -> assemble, configure, establish, instantiate) Tj
T*
(   - "point out" -> indicate, observe, note, highlight) Tj
T*
(   - "bring about" -> induce, elicit, cause, precipitate) Tj
T*
(   - "turn into" -> convert, transform, differentiate) Tj
T*
(   - "rule out" -> exclude, eliminate, discount) Tj
T*
(   - "give off" -> emit, release, discharge) Tj
T*
(   - "back up" -> corroborate, substantiate, validate) Tj
T*
(   - "put forward" -> propose, postulate, hypothesize) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
