(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the syntactic mechanics of separable versus inseparable phrasal verbs in technical writing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Syntactic Separation Property:) Tj
T*
(   Phrasal verbs vary based on whether an intervening direct object can be positioned between the) Tj
T*
(   lexical verb and its accompanying particle:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Separable Phrasal Verbs \(Transitive\):) Tj
T*
(   - Particle Placement: The direct object may appear either after the particle OR between the) Tj
T*
(   verb and the particle:) Tj
T*
(   - "The laboratory technician carried out the protocol." \(Post-particle\).) Tj
T*
(   - "The laboratory technician carried the protocol out." \(Intervening\).) Tj
T*
(   - Mandatory Separation with Pronouns: When the direct object is a personal pronoun, it MUST be) Tj
T*
(   placed between the verb and particle:) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "The technician carried it out.") Tj
T*
(   - Ungrammatical: "*The technician carried out it.") Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "We set them up." \(Not *We set up them\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Inseparable Phrasal Verbs \(Prepositional Verbs\):) Tj
T*
(   - Inseparable: The lexical verb and preposition form an indivisible syntactic unit; the direct) Tj
T*
(   object can NEVER split them:) Tj
T*
(   - "The researchers looked into the mutation.") Tj
T*
(   - Ungrammatical: "*The researchers looked the mutation into.") Tj
T*
(   - Ungrammatical with Pronoun: "*The researchers looked it into.") Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "The researchers looked into it.") Tj
T*
(   - Examples of Inseparable Verbs: adhere to, account for, cope with, rely on, dispose of.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze precision in biotechnology terminology, distinguishing between 'sterilization', 'disinfection', 'antisepsis', and 'sanitization'.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Critical Decontamination Taxonomy:) Tj
T*
(   Imprecise usage of decontamination terms in standard operating procedures \(SOPs\) can compromise) Tj
T*
(   cleanroom safety, invalidate clinical validations, or violate FDA/cGMP compliance:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Rigorous Scientific Definitions:) Tj
T*
(   - Sterilization:) Tj
T*
(   - The absolute physical or chemical elimination or destruction of ALL viable forms of microbial) Tj
T*
(   life, including bacterial endospores and viruses:) Tj
T*
(   - Methodologies: Autoclaving at 121 deg C \(15 psi\) for 15-30 minutes, gamma irradiation,) Tj
T*
(   ethylene oxide gas.) Tj
T*
(   - Benchmark: Zero microbial survival probability \(Sterility Assurance Level 10^-6\).) Tj
T*
(   - Disinfection:) Tj
T*
ET

