(   - The destruction or chemical elimination of pathogenic microorganisms on INANIMATE surfaces) Tj
T*
(   \(benches, hoods, floors\):) Tj
T*
(   - Critical Distinction: Disinfection destroys vegetative bacteria but does NOT reliably destroy) Tj
T*
(   resistant bacterial endospores \(e.g., Bacillus or Clostridium spores\).) Tj
T*
(   - Agents: 70% ethanol, 10% sodium hypochlorite \(bleach\), quaternary ammonium compounds.) Tj
T*
(   - Antisepsis:) Tj
T*
(   - The application of non-toxic chemical agents directly to LIVING BIOLOGICAL TISSUE \(skin,) Tj
T*
(   mucous membranes\) to inhibit or arrest microbial proliferation:) Tj
T*
(   - Agents: Chlorhexidine gluconate, povidone-iodine, 70% isopropanol skin wipes.) Tj
T*
(   - Sanitization:) Tj
T*
(   - The reduction of microbial populations on surfaces to safe public health regulatory) Tj
T*
(   thresholds:) Tj
T*
(   - Context: Industrial bioprocessing food-grade washdowns.) Tj
