(   2. Detailed Definitions:) Tj
T*
(   - Complement \(with 'e' - To complete or enhance mutual functionality\):) Tj
T*
(   - As a Verb: To supply what is lacking to form a harmonious, integrated whole:) Tj
T*
(   - "The RNA-seq transcriptomic data complement our proteomic mass spectrometry findings.") Tj
T*
(   - As a Noun: An entity that completes another:) Tj
T*
(   - "DNA base pairs form complementary strands: adenine is the complement of thymine.") Tj
T*
(   - In Immunology: The 'Complement System' \(a cascade of serum proteases enhancing immune) Tj
T*
(   clearance\).) Tj
T*
(   - Compliment \(with 'i' - Praise or free courtesy\):) Tj
T*
(   - As a Verb: To express praise, admiration, or congratulation:) Tj
T*
(   - "The keynote speaker complimented the graduate students on their rigorous poster) Tj
T*
(   presentation.") Tj
T*
(   - As an Adjective \(Complimentary\): Given free of charge as a courtesy:) Tj
T*
(   - "The vendor supplied a complimentary sample of DNA ladder.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Diagnostic Memory Hook:) Tj
T*
(   ComplEment with an 'E' adds what is nEcessary to complEte.) Tj
