(   - Prove:) Tj
T*
(   - Absolute deductive certainty; completely eliminates alternative explanations.) Tj
T*
(   - Usage in Biology: Rarely appropriate for empirical findings; strictly reserved for) Tj
T*
(   mathematical or logical proofs:) Tj
T*
(   - Caution: Avoid "*These data prove our theory".) Tj
T*
(   - Demonstrate:) Tj
T*
(   - High empirical certainty based on direct, undeniable experimental observation:) Tj
T*
(   - "Cryo-EM reconstructions demonstrate that the ribosome undergoes conformational rotation.") Tj
T*
(   - Indicate:) Tj
T*
(   - Clear, strong evidentiary support without claiming absolute mathematical closure:) Tj
T*
(   - "Western blot analyses indicate elevated expression of target kinase.") Tj
T*
(   - Suggest:) Tj
T*
(   - Prudent scientific deduction; acknowledges that while the proposed interpretation is favored,) Tj
T*
(   alternative models remain plausible:) Tj
T*
(   - "These binding kinetics suggest that allosteric regulation is operative.") Tj
T*
(   - Imply:) Tj
T*
(   - Logical consequence that follows indirectly from empirical premises without being stated) Tj
T*
(   outright.) Tj
