(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the morphological meaning and diagnostic applications of the 'Omics' cascade in biotechnology.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Hierarchical Cascade of Molecular Biology:) Tj
T*
(   Modern systems biology conceptualizes cellular functioning through an integrated, multi-layered) Tj
T*
(   informational hierarchy:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Four Pillars of the 'Omics' Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Genomics:) Tj
T*
(   - Analyzes the complete DNA nucleotide sequence \(the genome\).) Tj
T*
(   - Technologies: Next-Generation Sequencing \(NGS\), PacBio, Oxford Nanopore.) Tj
T*
(   - Scope: Static genetic blueprint, SNPs, copy number variations, structural rearrangements.) Tj
T*
(   - Transcriptomics:) Tj
T*
(   - Quantifies the complete repertoire of RNA transcripts \(the transcriptome\) expressed under) Tj
T*
(   specific environmental conditions.) Tj
T*
(   - Technologies: RNA-seq, single-cell RNA-seq \(scRNA-seq\).) Tj
T*
(   - Scope: Dynamic gene expression, alternative splicing, non-coding RNAs.) Tj
T*
(   - Proteomics:) Tj
T*
(   - Identifies and quantifies the complete complement of proteins \(the proteome\), including) Tj
T*
(   post-translational modifications \(PTMs\).) Tj
T*
(   - Technologies: Tandem Mass Spectrometry \(LC-MS/MS\), Cryo-EM.) Tj
T*
(   - Scope: Enzymatic activity, phosphorylation, protein-protein interaction networks.) Tj
T*
(   - Metabolomics:) Tj
T*
(   - Profiles the complete pool of low-molecular-weight metabolites \(the metabolome\).) Tj
T*
(   - Technologies: Nuclear Magnetic Resonance \(NMR\), GC-MS.) Tj
T*
(   - Scope: Direct metabolic flux, biochemical phenotypic reality.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
