(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze phrasal verbs with 'bring' \('bring about', 'bring down', 'bring up'\) in research communications.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Formal Substitutions in Scientific Manuscripts:) Tj
T*
(   - Bring about:) Tj
T*
(   - Meaning: Causing an event or chemical transformation to occur.) Tj
T*
(   - Formal Replacement: Elicit, precipitate, induce, cause, trigger.) Tj
T*
(   - Example: "Thermal shock induced the expression of heat-shock chaperones.") Tj
T*
(   - Bring down:) Tj
T*
(   - Meaning: Decreasing temperature, pressure, or glucose levels.) Tj
T*
(   - Formal Replacement: Lower, reduce, attenuate, depress.) Tj
T*
(   - Example: "Insulin administration reduced blood glucose levels to normoglycemic thresholds.") Tj
T*
(   - Bring up:) Tj
T*
(   - Meaning: Mentioning a topic for discussion during an academic defense.) Tj
T*
(   - Formal Replacement: Broach, raise, introduce.) Tj
T*
(   - Example: "The thesis committee raised critical questions regarding vector safety.") Tj
T*
