12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine precision in technical quantitative adjectives: 'negligible', 'marginal', 'appreciable', 'substantial'.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Quantitative Calibrating Spectrum:) Tj
T*
(   When describing experimental effects, adjectives establish quantitative boundaries:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Adjective Continuum:) Tj
T*
(   - Negligible:) Tj
T*
(   - So small, trifling, or minute that it can be safely disregarded without affecting empirical) Tj
T*
(   conclusions:) Tj
T*
(   - "The background fluorescence signal in the blank well was negligible \(< 0.1%\).") Tj
T*
(   - Marginal:) Tj
T*
(   - At the very border of significance; minor, borderline, or barely discernible:) Tj
T*
(   - "The mutant strain displayed a marginal increase in ethanol tolerance \(p = 0.048\).") Tj
T*
(   - Appreciable:) Tj
T*
(   - Sufficiently large or distinct to be easily noticed, measured, or recognized:) Tj
T*
(   - "Western blot analysis revealed an appreciable accumulation of recombinant protein.") Tj
T*
(   - Substantial:) Tj
T*
(   - Considerably large, significant, robust, and meaningful:) Tj
T*
(   - "The CRISPR-engineered crop exhibited a substantial 40% increase in drought resilience.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
